  "summary": "The ~70 t crawler dozer clears vegetation, strips topsoil and overburden, rips the softer caprock and ore where blasting is not needed, builds and maintains ROM-pad stockpiles and haul-road edges, and shapes the landform for rehabilitation. A semi-U blade pushes material; a single-shank parallelogram ripper at the rear breaks hard ground to about 1–1.5 m depth.",
